WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.199
Good morning Hank, it's Friday, it's question
Friday, the day that I answer real questions

00:00:03.199 --> 00:00:04.390
from real nerdfighters.

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:07.979
Are there any words you still can't spell?
I occasionally struggle with occasionally.

00:00:07.979 --> 00:00:11.290
Also refrigerator, where is your "D" refrigerator?

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.440
Did you see that NASA tweeted Hank's video?
Yes I did! Hank, I'm glad you're not quite

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:19.330
as obsessed with space as you were when you
were 16, because that might have made your

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:20.419
brain explode.

00:00:20.419 --> 00:00:23.740
Wait in Hank's video he said that telescope
can see into the past. How can you see into

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:26.550
the past?
Okay so light travels at a speed, so if something

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:32.440
is 13 billion light-years away, what we see
when we look at it happened 13 billion years

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:37.430
ago because that's how long it took the light
to get to us. Similarly, our sun is like 8

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:41.870
light-minutes away from us so we have no idea
what is currently happening on the sun. All

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:47.420
of our sun-related news is at least 8 minutes
old. Which is why the sun needs a twitter,

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:49.520
Hank. That wouldn't work? Bummer.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.690
Which part of Will Grayson, Will Grayson did
you write?

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:54.990
Uppercase Will AKA straight Will AKA Schrödinger's
Will.

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:59.000
Hey do y'all fill up power steering fluid?
Sorry that was my question for Jiffy Lube.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.380
Who the eff is Hank?
Hank is a comic book superhero from the DC

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:07.310
Universe who first appeared in 1939. Hank
is also known as "The Caped Crusader" and

00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:08.310
"The Hank."

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:12.180
Where should I invest a small amount of money?
I recommend a broad index fund like the Wilshire

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:13.180
5000.

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:15.490
If you could live in any period of history,
which would it be?

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:19.280
This one. Why would anyone wanna live in a
period other than this one? Like I acknowledge

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:24.539
that Rome was fantastic and everything but
a nerd with 4 days on his hand can recreate

00:01:24.539 --> 00:01:27.109
Rome in its entirety in Minecraft.

00:01:27.109 --> 00:01:30.979
What are those blue creatures behind you?
There are blue creatures behind me? Do they

00:01:30.979 --> 00:01:34.240
look menacing? You can't answer you're inside
the internet. I'm just gonna have to turn

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:41.520
around and face the music. Oh those guys?!
These were sewn for me by a nerdfighter. Possibly

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:43.700
they were supposed to be a present for Henry,
but anyway I took them.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:46.630
Peeta or Gale?
I am with the bakers!

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:50.130
Do you use hair product?
No. The puff needs hair product like Hank

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:51.130
needs caffeine.

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:53.579
What's your overall stance on the Israeli/Palestinian
conflict?

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:57.460
My overall stance is that both sides need
to recognize the legitimacy of the other's

00:01:57.460 --> 00:01:58.460
narrative.

00:01:58.460 --> 00:02:02.390
Will your zombie novella ever be published?
It was released under a creative commons license

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:06.520
so it is freely available all over the internet
 - link in the dooblydoo. However, before

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:10.539
you download it you are ethically obligated
to leave a comment thanking all the people

00:02:10.539 --> 00:02:15.350
who donated because without them this terrible
zombie novella would not exist. Also you have

00:02:15.350 --> 00:02:18.640
to promise to read one of my actual books
 - link in the dooblydoo - so you don't believe

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:21.680
that I'm as bad a writer as my zombie novella
would indicate.

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:25.319
Why do we have eyelids?
I don't know; blinking is for COWARDS.

00:02:25.319 --> 00:02:30.209
When you and Hank play clue, who is Mr. Green?
So Hank in the original British Cluedo, Mr.

00:02:30.209 --> 00:02:33.379
Green is called Reverend Green but when they
brought it to America they felt like that

00:02:33.379 --> 00:02:36.959
was sacrilege - sacrilege, by the way, is
another word I have trouble spelling. So they

00:02:36.959 --> 00:02:39.319
renamed him Mr. Green, but anyway I'm usually
Colonel Mustard.

00:02:39.319 --> 00:02:43.430
What English word retains its pronunciation
even after you take away 4 of its 5 letters?

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:47.560
Queue. Another word I have trouble spelling.
This is like the John Green Spelling Bee Nightmare

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:49.060
Edition of Question Friday.

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:51.370
What's your bracelet?
It's an Esther bracelet! You don't have an

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:55.300
Esther bracelet? You should get one, they
make the world suck less! Link in the dooblydoo.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.319
Why was Henry crying at the end of your last
video?

00:02:57.319 --> 00:03:00.900
That is not a question that was asked by a
parent. There is no "why." Like pretty much

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:05.560
the only two thoughts babies ever have are
"I am ecstatically happy," and "this could

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:10.430
be better." And they really only have one
strategy to take things from "this could be

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:13.620
better" to "I am ecstatically happy," which
is crying.

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:16.370
Why is a bubble round?
Because they're minimal surface structures,

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:17.959
and spheres have minimal surface.

00:03:17.959 --> 00:03:22.260
How's your Warner Chilcott stock doing?
Thank you for asking, I'm down $32. Warner

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:26.500
Chilcott you need to do a better job of Warner
Chilcott-ing sick people or else I'm never

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:27.500
gonna get my money back.

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:29.459
Can I be your last question?
Almost.

00:03:29.459 --> 00:03:32.410
Will you see Hank on Monday?
YES!

00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:36.019
By the way, Hank, if you want an awesome gold
eagle shirt from our friend the Whomping Willow,

00:03:36.019 --> 00:03:37.710
link in the dooblydoo.

